From f02ad5169e0af1af3d899b44b29a3276db50f1b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 00:50:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 31/71] fix-juice-6: J-1 to J-5 in the Juice drawer, the card
 badge and the chart's tips

J-1 each tax part on its own line, named as the country names it (provincial tax, regional and
municipal surcharges, National Insurance, CPP and EI; a US row stays state or local tax), the
first form that fits one line. J-2 the household's tax line says how that country taxes one
earner ("Canada taxes each person on their own pay, as if single"), and the household line and
tips say the other adult is not working. J-3 Monthly/Yearly is kept in localStorage like the
household. J-4 the grades say what they mean in the badge, the score's tip and the Juice text;
plainer Clusters/Ranges tips; the edge chips say which edge. J-5 the card names the graded place
first, and the badge's tip and accessible name say the place. Tax numbers unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_014jaqot5Ddmi7Co6CofBiyc
